{# The Q Function #}
<section>
    <h2>The q() Function</h2>

    <p>The <code>q()</code> function is your primary tool for applying Q units:</p>

    <div class="code-block"><pre><code>@use "unit.gl" as *;

// Basic usage
.element {
  padding: q(16); // 1rem (16 × 0.0625rem)
  margin: q(8); // 0.5rem
  gap: q(24); // 1.5rem
  border-width: q(1); // 0.0625rem (≈1px)
}

// Negative values
.pull-up {
  margin-top: q(-8); // -0.5rem
}

// Calculations
.calculated {
  width: calc(100% - q(32));
}</code></pre></div>

    <h3>Common Values</h3>

    <div class="number-grid" style="margin: calc(var(--grid-unit) * 3) 0;">
        {% for q in [1, 2, 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96, 128] %}
        <div class="number-cell">
            <div class="number-cell__value">{{ q }}</div>
            <div class="number-cell__label">{{ q }}px</div>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</section>
